---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const p='/equipment/14-11/';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Accelerated soak witness" wide={true} subtitle="" description="Compare package-specific impedance and condition histories without inferring lifetime."><script is:inline>window.soakModule=import('/equipment/14-11/bench.mjs');</script><article class="equipment" id="soak">
<nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/14-11/">← Equipment 14-11</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#sw-ref">References</a><a href="#sw-proof">Verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">14-11 / RELIABILITY WITNESS</p><h2>Which package actually changed?</h2><p class="eq-lede">Record day 14 at 1 kHz. The paired inert specimens start with identical spectra. Package B gains 10% at that bin; package A and the other frequencies stay unchanged.</p></header>
<div class="soak-grid"><section><p class="eq-meta">01 / BATH ARRAY</p><h3>BTS Soak Witness Mk I</h3><div id="sw-view" aria-label="3D dual-bath fixture and impedance logger"></div><small id="sw-model" role="status">Loading metric model…</small><div class="tools"><button id="sw-far">Whole fixture</button><button id="sw-near">Inspect sample bay</button><button id="sw-cover">Open inspection cover</button><button id="sw-conn">Unplug package B</button></div><p>Drag or pinch to inspect. The cover, A and B electrical plugs and logger screen are operable mesh targets. Open the cover to change a connection; close it and connect the selected specimen before recording.</p></section>
<section><p class="eq-meta">02 / WITNESS LOG</p><h3>Compare with its own baseline</h3><div class="fields"><label>Bath and package<select id="sw-bath"><option value="0">A / PKG-A</option><option value="1" selected>B / PKG-B</option></select></label><label>Elapsed exposure<select id="sw-elapsedDays">{[0,3,7,14].map(d=><option value={d} selected={d===14}>Day {d}</option>)}</select></label><label>Frequency<select id="sw-hz"><option value="1000">1 kHz</option></select></label><label>Logged temperature (°C)<input id="sw-temp" value="60" type="number" min="20" max="80" step="any"/></label><label>Injected day-14 B / 1 kHz drift (%)<input id="sw-drift" value="10" type="number" min="-40" max="40" step="any"/></label></div>
<div class="tools"><button class="run" id="sw-run">Record witness</button><button id="sw-reset">Reset example</button></div><p id="sw-status" role="status">Ready to record.</p><p id="sw-replayState"></p><details><summary>Replay a simulated 09-01 spectrum</summary><p>Use the original exported EIS fixture or select an equivalent <a href="/simulations/equipment/09-01/simulator/">09-01</a> EIS JSON. This is baseline replay, not data from the bath or an aged specimen. Only a paired matched observation supports drift.</p><button id="sw-fixture">Load 09-01 baseline</button><label>Import simulator EIS JSON<input id="sw-import" type="file" accept=".json,application/json"/></label></details></section></div>
<section><p class="eq-meta">03 / CONDITION HISTORY</p><h3>Selected spectral bin</h3><p id="sw-result" aria-live="polite"></p><canvas id="sw-plot" width="590" height="190" aria-label="Magnitude drift by elapsed day"></canvas><div class="over"><table><thead><tr><th>Day</th><th>UTC date</th><th>Bath</th><th>°C</th><th>|Z|, Ω</th><th>Δ%, same sample</th></tr></thead><tbody id="sw-rows"></tbody></table></div><div class="tools"><button id="sw-export" disabled>Export condition and impedance JSON</button></div></section>
<section id="sw-ref"><p class="eq-meta">04 / BASIS</p><h3>Original geometry, documented measurement practice</h3><p>This first-pass fixture is a new virtual instrument. Its dimensions are design choices, not measured. The editable model has a 620 × 365 mm base, two nominal 226 × 198 mm bath blocks, fixed probe and rack locations, and an illustrative cover opening of 75°. Temperature and saline fraction are logged values. No real heater performance, ingress barrier or bath flow is represented.</p><p><a href="https://usbr.gov/tsc/techreferences/mands/mands-pdfs/ElectrochemicalImpedanceMethods_8540-2019-03_508.pdf">U.S. Bureau of Reclamation: electrochemical impedance for coated inert metal coupons</a> motivates logging conditioning and inspecting frequency-resolved Z. <a href="https://saliterman.umn.edu/sites/saliterman.umn.edu/files/files/general/gamry_instruments_basics_of_electrochemical_impedance_spectroscopy_eis.pdf">Gamry’s EIS note</a> describes the real/imaginary and magnitude/phase representation. The fitted scene is original, not derived from a manufacturer photograph or qualified physical hardware.</p>
<div class="tools"><a href={p+'build-model.py'} download>Editable Blender source</a><a href={p+'soak-witness.glb'} download>Download GLB</a><a href={p+'xr.json'}>Geometry checks and VR action targets</a><a href={p+'bench.mjs'}>Solver and station state</a><a href={p+'example.json'}>Download example report</a></div><p>World scale is metres; bath-cover hinge, labeled connectors and logger expose reusable ray targets and DOM-free actions. Orbit and pointer interaction here, not a verified physical headset session.</p></section>
<section id="sw-proof"><p class="eq-meta">05 / INDEPENDENT CHECKS</p><h3>Identity and frequency come first</h3><p>Witness records preserve package ID, ordered contact pair, acquisition revision, UTC timestamp, elapsed days and bath conditions. The synthetic baseline is a 12 kΩ resistor in parallel with 5 nF: Z=R/(1+j2πfRC). One deliberately injected gain changes both components of Z by the same factor, so phase is unchanged. That selective injection checks analysis isolation; it is not a mechanism or fit for water ingress.</p><p>Magnitude drift is 100(|Z<sub>current</sub>|/|Z<sub>base</sub>|−1), with phase wrapped to [−180°, 180°). Compare exactly matching frequencies and package/contact pairs. No interpolation, accelerated-time conversion, clinical lifetime, chemical response or corrosion derivation. Temperature changes the logged conditions, not the curve.</p>
<div class="over"><table><thead><tr><th>Independent test (default day 14)</th><th>Expected</th><th>Computed</th><th>Tolerance</th></tr></thead><tbody>{[['PKG-B 1 kHz','+10%','+10%'],['PKG-A 1 kHz','0%','0%'],['Both packages at 100 Hz and 10 kHz','0%','0%'],['Phase change on all bins','0°','0°']].map(([k,e,a])=><tr><th>{k}</th><td>{e}</td><td>{a}</td><td>Pass · 10⁻⁹ in declared units</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p>Zero baseline, absent bin, wrong contact identity and open/disconnected fixture are rejected. <a href={p+'gamry-baseline.json'}>Exact 09-01 example export</a> is verified independently for signed components and contact preservation. A snapshot is explicitly rendered as baseline-only. Report schema <code>bts.soak-report.v1</code> exports the selected delta, matching spectra and their sample condition history; a snapshot uses <code>baselineOnly: true</code> and its self-comparison is not evidence of drift.</p></section>
</article></Layout><script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/14-11/client.mjs';</script><style is:global>
#soak .soak-grid,#soak .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.15fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:.7rem}#soak section{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:1rem;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}#soak .soak-grid section{margin:0}#soak .eq-meta{margin:0}#soak h3{margin:.35rem 0 .7rem;font-size:1.5rem}#soak .tools{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:.45rem;margin:.65rem 0}#soak label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;box-sizing:border-box;min-width:0}#soak button,#soak input,#soak select{min-height:40px;font:inherit;max-width:100%;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel,transparent);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem;box-sizing:border-box}#soak button{cursor:pointer}#soak button.run{color:white;background:#365d5d}#soak button:disabled{opacity:.45}#sw-view{height:clamp(270px,30vw,415px);background:#283538}#sw-view canvas{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;touch-action:none}#sw-plot{width:min(100%,670px);height:auto;display:block}#soak .over{overflow:auto}#soak table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}#soak td,#soak th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}#sw-result{font-weight:bold}@media(max-width:760px){#soak .soak-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}#soak section{padding:.7rem}}
</style>
